Question Title: Advanced File Management

Question Link:
https://my.newtonschool.co/playground/code/4ks5o139cfoh?lecture_hash=v210chxjexei

Solution:
mkdir project-files
cd project-files
touch report.docx summary.docx draft.docx
cp report.docx report_backup.docx
mkdir old
mv draft.docx old/
mv summary.docx final_summary.docx
cp final_summary.docx old/
rm -rf report_backup.docx

Approach:
1. Create a folder called project-files.

2. Inside it, create three files: report.docx,summary.docx,draft.docx

3. Make a copy of report.docx and name it report_backup.docx.

4. Create a new folder called old. Move draft.docx into old/.

5. Rename summary.docx to final_summary.docx.

6. Copy final_summary.docx into the old/ folder as well.

7. Delete report_backup.docx.

Result:
project-files/
├── report.docx
├── final_summary.docx
└── old/
    ├── draft.docx
    └── final_summary.docx
file structure obtained